A weather forecast gives the probability of rain on Monday as $0.65$ and on Tuesday as $0.25$, and the two days are independent.
On the probability tree, $R$ means rain and $D$ means dry.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.95]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (N1) at (2.2,1.4);
\coordinate (N2) at (2.2,-1.4);
\coordinate (E1) at (4.8,2.4);
\coordinate (E2) at (4.8,0.7);
\coordinate (E3) at (4.8,-0.7);
\coordinate (E4) at (4.8,-2.4);
\draw (O) -- (N1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.65$};
\draw (O) -- (N2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$?$};
\draw (N1) -- (E1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.25$};
\draw (N1) -- (E2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.75$};
\draw (N2) -- (E3) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.25$};
\draw (N2) -- (E4) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.75$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N1) {$R$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N2) {$D$};
\node[right] at (E1) {$R$};
\node[right] at (E2) {$D$};
\node[right] at (E3) {$R$};
\node[right] at (E4) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which decimal belongs on the branch marked $?$

Kofi makes a free throw $\frac{3}{7}$ of the time, and his shots are independent.
He takes two free throws, where $M$ means made and $X$ means missed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.95]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (N1) at (2.2,1.4);
\coordinate (N2) at (2.2,-1.4);
\coordinate (E1) at (4.8,2.4);
\coordinate (E2) at (4.8,0.7);
\coordinate (E3) at (4.8,-0.7);
\coordinate (E4) at (4.8,-2.4);
\draw (O) -- (N1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{3}{7}$};
\draw (O) -- (N2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{4}{7}$};
\draw (N1) -- (E1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{3}{7}$};
\draw (N1) -- (E2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{4}{7}$};
\draw (N2) -- (E3) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{3}{7}$};
\draw (N2) -- (E4) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{4}{7}$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N1) {$M$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N2) {$X$};
\node[right] at (E1) {$M$};
\node[right] at (E2) {$X$};
\node[right] at (E3) {$M$};
\node[right] at (E4) {$X$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the probability that he makes both free throws?

A machine has two components that operate independently, and each works with probability $\frac{5}{9}$.
On the probability tree, $W$ means works and $F$ means fails.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.95]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (N1) at (2.2,1.4);
\coordinate (N2) at (2.2,-1.4);
\coordinate (E1) at (4.8,2.4);
\coordinate (E2) at (4.8,0.7);
\coordinate (E3) at (4.8,-0.7);
\coordinate (E4) at (4.8,-2.4);
\draw (O) -- (N1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{5}{9}$};
\draw (O) -- (N2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{4}{9}$};
\draw (N1) -- (E1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{5}{9}$};
\draw (N1) -- (E2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{4}{9}$};
\draw (N2) -- (E3) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{5}{9}$};
\draw (N2) -- (E4) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{4}{9}$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N1) {$W$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N2) {$F$};
\node[right] at (E1) {$W$};
\node[right] at (E2) {$F$};
\node[right] at (E3) {$W$};
\node[right] at (E4) {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the probability that both components fail?

A weather forecast gives the probability of rain on Saturday as $0.25$ and on Sunday as $0.4$, and the two days are independent.
On the probability tree, $R$ means rain and $D$ means dry.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.95]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (N1) at (2.2,1.4);
\coordinate (N2) at (2.2,-1.4);
\coordinate (E1) at (4.8,2.4);
\coordinate (E2) at (4.8,0.7);
\coordinate (E3) at (4.8,-0.7);
\coordinate (E4) at (4.8,-2.4);
\draw (O) -- (N1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.25$};
\draw (O) -- (N2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.75$};
\draw (N1) -- (E1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.4$};
\draw (N1) -- (E2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.6$};
\draw (N2) -- (E3) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.4$};
\draw (N2) -- (E4) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$0.6$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N1) {$R$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N2) {$D$};
\node[right] at (E1) {$R$};
\node[right] at (E2) {$D$};
\node[right] at (E3) {$R$};
\node[right] at (E4) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the probability that it rains on exactly one of the two days?
